# Where am I
> In the AmigaDOS Shell you type **Dir** to list a drawer and **CD** to move into one.
> In vsh the same jobs are done by `ls`, `cd` and `pwd`.
> Type each command at the `tutorial>` prompt, as you would at the vsh prompt.
$ mkdir docs
$ touch docs/a.txt
? Print the list of files here (AmigaDOS: Dir). The command is ls.
= grep -q docs "$LEARN_OUT"
~ Type ls and press Return.
! ls
> `pwd` prints the drawer you are in (AmigaDOS: CD with no argument).
? Print where you are.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in *pwd*) true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type pwd.
! pwd
> `cd NAME` moves into a drawer, as AmigaDOS CD does.
? Go into the drawer docs.
= [ "${PWD##*/}" = docs ]
~ Type cd docs.
! cd docs
> `..` is the parent drawer (AmigaDOS: a lone slash). A lone `/` lists the volumes, and
> `~` is your home drawer, $HOME (SYS: unless you changed it).
? Go back to the parent drawer.
= [ "${PWD##*/}" != docs ]
~ Type cd .. (a space between cd and the two dots).
! cd ..
